  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1017 PM MDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nUpper high will stretch across the southern tier of the CONUS \nTuesday but the high gets dissolved and then redevelops itself over \nthe desert southwest Wednesday. This upper high looks to persist in \nthis area through Friday. Thunderstorm chances will persist each \nafternoon focusing over the area mountains and western NM locations \nof the CWA. More isolated to scattered activity in the desert \nlowlands. Biggest threats with storms will be gusty outflow winds \nand moderate to heavy rainfall which could lead to flooding. Friday \nstill looks to be a downtick in activity, mostly just focusing over \nthe mountains and far western NM locations with hardly any storms in \nthe lowlands. A couple of passing troughs over the northern CONUS \nwill mostly dissolve the high over the area and would bring some \npotential for better areawide rain chances Sunday and Monday.",
